Subject: test: a quit during a pin's question, and the DRM test with sign-in
 off

The browser test that counts requests ran with the test suite's pretended
OAuth client, so browser sign-in was allowed and the profile could ask
accounts.google.com which accounts it holds, on its own time. On a slow
build that landed in the middle of the count. It now runs as a Stedding
build does. A fresh profile of the real build sent no such request in 75
seconds.

A quit begun while a pin's page asks "Leave site?" had a test only for a
window close. The quit's own path waits for the same answer.

Why: BACKLOG S-443 and S-435; docs/features/pins.md H3, privacy Q12.

Removable when: never as a test.
---
 .../test/stedding/drm_notice_browsertest.cc   |  6 +++
 .../stedding/sidebar_click_browsertest.cc     | 51 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 57 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/test/stedding/drm_notice_browsertest.cc b/chrome/test/stedding/drm_notice_browsertest.cc
index 07104fbe99f8f..0cda8a3af4d12 100644
--- a/chrome/test/stedding/drm_notice_browsertest.cc
+++ b/chrome/test/stedding/drm_notice_browsertest.cc
@@ -147,6 +147,12 @@ class DrmNoticeTest : public InProcessBrowserTest {
   void SetUpCommandLine(base::CommandLine* command_line) override {
     InProcessBrowserTest::SetUpCommandLine(command_line);
     mock_cert_verifier_.SetUpCommandLine(command_line);
+    // Browser sign-in is not allowed, as in a Stedding build. The test suite
+    // pretends an OAuth client exists (ChromeTestSuite), so without this the
+    // profile may ask accounts.google.com which accounts it holds, on its own
+    // time, and on a slow build that lands in the middle of a test that counts
+    // requests (BACKLOG S-443).
+    command_line->AppendSwitchASCII("allow-browser-signin", "false");
   }
 
   void SetUpInProcessBrowserTestFixture() override {
